From: Q1000K development <q1000k@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: model vendor PON transport as an internal link

The Q1000K vendor PHY owns the optical PCS registers. GDM2 is only the
CPU DMA endpoint, so its phylink must not wait for the competing native
PON PCS. The existing board/SoC/port checks restrict pon_port to Q1000K
GDM2. Its fixed link indicates transport availability, not optical state.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -4023,10 +4023,11 @@ static int airoha_setup_phylink(struct net_device *netdev)
 	config->type = PHYLINK_NETDEV;
 
 	/*
-	 * GDM1 only supports internal for Embedded Switch
-	 * and doesn't require a PCS.
+	 * GDM1 connects the embedded switch. The vendor PON endpoint
+	 * connects CPU DMA to a separately managed optical PHY/MAC.
+	 * Neither internal transport requires a native PCS.
 	 */
-	if (port->id == AIROHA_GDM1_IDX) {
+	if (port->id == AIROHA_GDM1_IDX || dev->pon_port) {
 		config->mac_capabilities = MAC_ASYM_PAUSE | MAC_SYM_PAUSE |
 					   MAC_10000FD;
 
